+- `src/schemas/contract.ts`: a copy of contract 1.6 from backend 1.5 (`npm run check-schema`: two `SAME`).
+- `src/api.ts`: eleven fleet functions (see "What's in the `src/` folder"). `src/types.ts`: the types of the fleet, releases, updates, claim codes, the Socket.IO `ota` event, and the `ota`/`provisioning`/`revoked` event kinds.
+- `src/socket.ts`: the `ota` event to the store; the `provisioning`/`revoked` events fetch the device list and the fleet again; the toast colors of `ota`, `provisioning`, and `offline-mode`; a restored connection fetches the fleet again too. `src/store.ts`: `ota`, `receiveOta()`, `fleetVersion`, `fleetChanged()`.
+- `src/App.tsx`: the `/fleet` route (admin and viewer). `src/components/Layout.tsx`: the **Fleet** menu; a name and **Log out** that move down a row are right-aligned from 640 px (`sm:ml-auto`).
+- `src/components/Badge.tsx`, `DeviceDetails.tsx`, `DeviceList.tsx`, `src/map.ts`: `offline-mode` = **stopped on purpose** (sky blue), no longer "offline mode".
+- `vite.config.ts`: `/fw` joins `navigateFallbackDenylist` (the service worker never answers `/fw/…` with `index.html`).
+- `caddy/Caddyfile` (the infrastructure part of Module 28): the `handle /fw/*` block to the backend, an `encode` that doesn't compress `/fw/*`, `servers :80` (the `X-Forwarded-For` trust only on door 80), and the device door `:8081`. `Dockerfile`: comments only (tag 1.4.0).
+- Fixes after the code verification (still 1.4.0, not yet published): a button's error on the device card and the release card (Update, Canary, interval, Deactivate, Update canary/all) stays on the card until **Close** (`components/ErrorBox.tsx`), not a 4-second toast, because the `503` of Deactivate says to repeat the step; after "are you sure?" the focus moves to the reason sentence of a button that is now disabled, and after Deactivate to the **Close** of the steps box; the upload form refuses a version with a leading zero (`1.07.1`), the same as backend 1.5.
+
 ## Version 1.3 notes
 
 Dashboard v1.3 (Module 27) = v1.2 + an installed app (PWA). One new developer package, no screen changes; the data contract stays the same (the message shapes are the same as in 1.4; contract 1.5 only adds the internet broker rules). Its partner on the internet is backend 1.4 (`TRUST_PROXY`: `Secure` cookies and a per-visitor login limiter behind Caddy); at `http://localhost` v1.3 also runs with backend 1.3, except that the failed-command toast ("… if it hears from the device within 2 minutes") is only right with backend 1.4; backend 1.3 still sends that command again whenever the device is heard again.
